welcome to max tech and this is our six  month review of the ipad mini 6.  [Music]  it's been over six months since apple  released the ipad mini 6 and i've got to  be honest with you guys this is by far  my favorite ipad for doing ipad things  now when i say that i'm separating ipad  things and professional things because  the 11 inch ipad pro is by far a much  better ipad in terms of also being a  professional laptop replacement but if  you're just trying to get an ipad and  enjoying it for consuming media watching  movies watching shows playing games or  just browsing the web surfing through  twitter or whatever else this is where  it's at now i know that might surprise  you because the new ipad air 5 was just  released and it has a bunch of upgrades  including the famed m1 chip but i  actually like this better now before i  explain all the reasons why i want to  get into my experience or my thoughts on  the ipad mini 6 after six months now the  two things that really set this ipad  mini 6 apart from the other ipads in the  lineup are first of all the compact size  with the new redesign and of course  number two is the price you can get this  thing for 500 so you're saving money  compared to the higher end ipads and it  has just about the perfect size for an  ipad doing all those things like  consuming media and of course it has the  new redesign which is super super nice  compared to the budget ipad which is  still using that old home button design  i absolutely love basically every single  part of the design of the ipad mini  first of all those flat sides the  thickness is just perfect for holding it  the speaker grilles on both the top and  bottom look really good you got the  volume buttons on top including the new  touch id power button which honestly i  don't prefer that compared to face id on  the ipad pro but of course this is a  much cheaper device and hopefully in the  future apple does bring face id to the  ipad mini going around to the back i  really love how you have that single  camera design you've got the flash which  of course the new ipad air still doesn't  have and just overall everything is just  so proportionate and of course you got  the usbc port which is a huge upgrade  compared to lighting i mean this is the  cheapest way to get a usbc port on an  ipad and it just works so well and where  i think apple absolutely nailed it is  the compact size because this is not  only perfect for me for consuming media  having a larger display than on an  iphone and just holding in your hands  like this super comfortable you can type  or you can hold it in landscape mode  just so much comfort for doing things  like gaming but the real sweet spot is  when it comes to children if you have  kids this is the perfect size i let my  son use this about six months ago when  he was still only one year old then he  was able to hold it in his hands and  watch some movies or some cartoons  perfectly fine as a little kid a little  one-year-old and now my favorite part  about this ipad mini is that it comes  with the latest a15 bionic chip with the  five core gpu which means it packs a ton  of graphics power and overall processing  power inside of it which means that if  you buy this ipad mini you're gonna be  good for the next five or plus years  because it handles basically every app  and game with ease and it doesn't heat  up it's just so impressive and in terms  of gaming support this is actually very  impressive because you can play any game  at perfect 60 fps and just to prove it  to you guys look at golden reviewers  tests of ganshin impact which is by far  the most demanding ios or ipad os game  and he basically got a perfect 60 fps  beating out all of the other mobile  phones including the iphone 13 pro max  because this thing is able to stay cool  enough for the chip to run at full  performance giving you perfect solid 60  fps so that means any game you play is  gonna run perfectly smoothly on this  ipad mini which makes it so good and in  terms of usability while gaming  this is literally the perfect size for  gaming you hold it in your hands it's  like having a game controller you can  fit everything your thumbs all across  the screen it's just so convenient  especially with the new redesign they  got rid of the chin on the bottom and  the forehead so now you have unified  bezels all the way around and it makes  the controls  for moving in shooting or attacking  closer to the edge which makes it a lot  more convenient now with that said  you're probably wondering about the ipad  air 5 because that just got the m1 chip  now of course it is a lot more powerful  than the a15 in this ipad mini however  it has a huge drawback even though it  has the m1 chip it still only has a 60hz  display just like this ipad mini and  what that means is all of the extra  performance on top of the a15 is  completely wasted when you're doing  things like gaming because this already  hits 60 fps perfect performance with the  a15 so what's the point of the m1 plus  you have the larger ipad air size which  is less convenient to hold in your hand  for gaming so honestly the extra m1 chip  on the ipad air doesn't really matter  and i think going all the way up to the  ipad pro makes a lot more sense because  you get the 120hz pro motion display so  if you want to spend more money than 500  bucks for this ipad mini 6 then just go  straight for the ipad pro and making  this even better this is actually on  sale right now for 460 bucks on amazon  using the link in the pinned comment  below this is just such a crazy deal for  what you get basically the best mobile  gaming device out there now in terms of  the other ways the ipad mini compares to  the ipad air well first of all this  thing comes with a flash which the ipad  air does not and it basically comes with  the same camera system 12 megapixels on  the back and the same 12 megapixel ultra  wide on the front so no real differences  there the main advantage of the ipad air  is actually the usb type c port which is  twice as fast supporting 10 gigabit per  second transfers compared to 5 but for a  lot of people that may not be a big deal  especially if you're using this as an  ipad mainly and one thing i really like  about this redesign is this new folio  case which actually attaches  magnetically which i absolutely love yes  apple packed in magnets into the ipad  mini so you don't have anything wrapping  around the sides super convenient you  just plop on your apple pencil if you  choose to have one and it's just  basically the perfect all-around design  now on top of everything i already  mentioned i do want to reiterate that  this thing is an excellent media  consumption device yes that means  watching youtube videos streaming apple  tv plus hbo max netflix if you're still  subscribed to that maybe who knows but  the display on this is just perfect the  speakers you have on both sides you have  landscape stereo mode so overall  for being an ipad and using it as an  ipad like on your couch anywhere else  taking it with you on the go this is  just so compact the size is perfect for  your hands perfect for your kids hands  i just love this ipad i've got to say  this is my favorite ipad for ipad use so  with that said hopefully you enjoyed  this video and if you did go ahead and  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one but if you  disagree with me if you think a  different ipad is better let me know in  the comments section below and make sure  to check out one of those two videos  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]
 

